  "text_md": "# <u>DEFINITIONS</u>\n\n## Categories of Need\n\n|||Residential Services|Services to people who require some degree|\n|---|---|---|---|\n|||(Not including|of staffing support to maintain them in their|\n|Emergency|Persons needing services immediately.|24 hour staff)|home, but do not require staffing on a 24 hour/day continuous basis.|\n|Critical|Persons needing services within one year.|||\n|Planning For|Persons with needs more than one year away.||The 12 month period from July 1 to June 30 on which Commonwealth budgets are based. The basic foundation that must be in place for an organization to function properly|\n|High Intensity|Persons receiving residential services, possibly in addition to vocational/day services, ancillary/support services, and case management||(administrative, information systems, staffing). Prioritization of Urgency of Need for Services for Persons with Mental Retardation—Data|\n|Medium Intensity|Persons receiving vocational/day services, possibly in addition to support/ancillary services and case management||collection instrument developed by Temple University to assess the need of individuals waiting for services.|\n|Low Intensity|Persons receiving support or ancillary services|||\n\n## Fiscal Year\n\n## Categories of Service Infrastructure\n\n## PUNS\n\n(therapies, F.S.S., transportation), in addition to case management services **Types of Service** Day Services Non-residential services to people with mental retardation including adult developmentaltraining, vocational rehabilitation, and community employment Residential Services Services necessary to maintain a person in (24 hour staff) their home or in some other residential setting by providing staffing support 24 hours a day.\n",
